    <h1>Facing Criminal or Immigration Proceedings in the Philippines?</h1>
    <p class="service-lede">Coordinated support when criminal and immigration matters intersect.</p>

    <p>Foreign nationals involved in criminal proceedings may also face separate immigration consequences, including visa, detention or deportation-related matters.</p>

    <p>Foreign Immigration Services can coordinate immigration-related assistance alongside independent Philippine legal counsel, who advise and represent clients directly in the relevant criminal or judicial proceedings. Where legal representation is required, we assist in coordinating with qualified legal partners so you have both sides — immigration and legal — working in step.</p>

    <h2>How We Can Assist</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Assessing the immigration-related consequences of your situation</li>
      <li>Coordinating with independent Philippine legal counsel on your behalf</li>
      <li>Keeping you informed of the immigration aspects of your matter as it progresses</li>
      <li>Acting promptly where a matter is time-sensitive</li>
    </ul>

    <div class="service-cta">
